# Trust Tasks — code ownership
#
# Each Trust Task specification lives in specs/<slug>/<version>/.
# Slugs may be hierarchical (multiple path segments separated by /),
# in which case the on-disk folder matches the slug (e.g. specs/acl/grant/).
# CODEOWNERS gives every spec namespace its own reviewer set so editors can
# manage their specifications independently. To add a new spec namespace:
#
#   1. Create the folder specs/<slug>/<version>/ with spec.md +
#      payload.schema.json (see CONTRIBUTING-SPECS.md).
#   2. Append a rule below pointing at the team or individual that
#      owns reviews for that slug or slug prefix.
#
# Until working-group teams exist in GitHub, individual specs default
# to the framework editor. Replace @stormer78 with @org/<team> when
# a team is set up.

# Default — anything not matched below
*                                  @stormer78

# Framework material
/SPEC.md                           @stormer78
/CONTRIBUTING.md                   @stormer78
/CONTRIBUTING-SPECS.md             @stormer78
/LICENSE.md                        @stormer78
/SOURCE_CODE.md                    @stormer78
/README.md                         @stormer78

# Build / deploy / tooling
/scripts/                          @stormer78
/.github/                          @stormer78
/package.json                      @stormer78
/specs/spec.meta.schema.json       @stormer78

# Website chrome (everything except the auto-synced specs/ tree)
/website/                          @stormer78
/website/specs/                    # generated by scripts/build-registry.mjs — no owner override needed

# Individual Trust Task namespaces — one rule per top-level slug segment.
# Replace @stormer78 with the editorial team for that namespace once it exists.
# A rule on /specs/acl/ covers every spec under that prefix
# (acl/grant, acl/revoke, acl/change-role, acl/list, acl/show).
/specs/acl/                        @stormer78

# Peer-to-peer relationship credentials and the witnessing that can accompany
# them — authored jointly with the DTG Core Credentials task force (see #173).
/specs/vrc/                        @stormer78
/specs/witness/                    @stormer78

# Framework-reserved response types: registry-published implementations
# of the slugs reserved by SPEC §6.1. Framework editors only.
/specs/trust-task-error/           @stormer78
/specs/trust-task-ok/              @stormer78
/specs/trust-task-next-step/       @stormer78
